<title>BRAZIL: Paranagua strike scheduled to end at 1300 today.</title>
<headline>Paranagua strike scheduled to end at 1300 today.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strike at the key Brazilian port of Paranagua was scheduled to end at 1300 local/1600 GMT Friday after dockworkers and port operators struck a deal over pay, the director of the dockworkers' union said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been resolved,&quot; said the official. &quot;We're going back to work at 1300.&quot;  </p>
<p>Portworkers at Paranagua have been on strike since midday Wednesday in support of dockworkers' demand for a 21 percent pay increase.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
